{"event_type":"review","id":"e9cafb420b3650ac8dec65277650f938f997d2d266c93becb6f5c806ce8da4e5","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T16:02:04Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c850eb5c5b58bb2f2eb53fca6c8f5406e2631677caf33654fd34b7ba11798338","sha256":"c850eb5c5b58bb2f2eb53fca6c8f5406e2631677caf33654fd34b7ba11798338"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4e84158e97b0fc7a96f2a044dc23d56bad0279e9a0b779790b1c585c25724859","sha256":"4e84158e97b0fc7a96f2a044dc23d56bad0279e9a0b779790b1c585c25724859"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5fa179580ee43b42171820b7c9abc8b0bf238f59401dd8263277c4582ee48c40","sha256":"5fa179580ee43b42171820b7c9abc8b0bf238f59401dd8263277c4582ee48c40"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6e933088b66eb897192ca84b9e3bcd7f80dbbd3e04e85a061de332e358d1c935","sha256":"6e933088b66eb897192ca84b9e3bcd7f80dbbd3e04e85a061de332e358d1c935"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f5e9838cf84c00f4d764bc76083e474ebd4c3c02aa1bea0719ea514cc2e9160c","sha256":"f5e9838cf84c00f4d764bc76083e474ebd4c3c02aa1bea0719ea514cc2e9160c"}],"attempt_id":"a0d5b6aaec560962b2164b7ee464e0b043a425c6545275fda30567b10b3ec64a:0:1","base":"d5f9293beeec28560ac6d385ff80b897633fce3b","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"60178b44c8cec37136530bb1f702e3e3ef91e6bc","body":"**Split `scanText` input on `\\r?\\n`. CRLF content can evade anchored rules.**\n\n`src/ops/dev/denylist.ts:298` splits on `'\\n'` only, so each line from CRLF content keeps a trailing `\\r`. In JavaScript, `.` does not match `\\r`, and `$` without the `m` flag matches only at end of input. A rule such as `token=.*$` therefore fails on `token=abc\\r`. A secret in a CRLF file or patch can pass the project-rule net.\n\nThe parser at Line 187 already uses `/\\r?\\n/`. The scan should use the same split. The 1-based line numbers do not change, because the split still happens on `\\n`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  const lines = text.split('\\n');\n+  const lines = text.split(/\\r?\\n/);\n```\n</details>\n\nThe script this module ports may handle `\\r` differently, because Python `.` matches `\\r`. Check the parity test for this case.","id":"cb5f3b885a6654a890d8ed1ff8a5ddacfa04076fdf4117e14925b17e1001919e","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/dev/denylist.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Split `scanText` input on `\\r?\\n`. CRLF content can evade anchored rules."}],"head":"c09f8c3e8e966ab1e4254d9fddb71f99cd9b84e5","head_tree":"b4ccd79a879cd59b7eca92377c3b119eff95db28","input_scope":[{"blob":"60178b44c8cec37136530bb1f702e3e3ef91e6bc","intervals":[[1,553]],"path":"src/ops/dev/denylist.ts"}],"job_id":"a0d5b6aaec560962b2164b7ee464e0b043a425c6545275fda30567b10b3ec64a:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"60178b44c8cec37136530bb1f702e3e3ef91e6bc","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/dev/denylist.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"60178b44c8cec37136530bb1f702e3e3ef91e6bc","intervals":[[60,60],[62,65]],"path":"src/ops/dev/denylist.ts"}],"reviewed_scope":[{"blob":"60178b44c8cec37136530bb1f702e3e3ef91e6bc","intervals":[[60,60],[62,65]],"path":"src/ops/dev/denylist.ts"}],"scope_digest":"52769bc2445e854f180430a1705de6b5582518ef986adba43903710615db47da","source":{"authenticated":true,"id":"backfill-a0d5b6aaec560962b2164b7ee464e0b043a425c6545275fda30567b10b3ec64a-g0-20261107T160030Z","producer":"crq-runner-app","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","type":"crq-run"},"subject_id":"a0d5b6aaec560962b2164b7ee464e0b043a425c